---
import { profile, harness, verify, sameSession } from "../data/profile";
---

<section id="claude" class="claude">
  <div class="wrap">
    <div class="section-head">
      <p class="eyebrow">04 · How I work with Claude Code</p>
      <h2>I don't hand Claude a task. I hand it a method.</h2>
      <p>
        I've used Claude Code every day since March 2025. It does most of the typing. I decide what
        gets built, how it gets checked, and when it stops. This page is a live example. My
        hand-coded portfolio from 2021 is still up at{" "}
        <a href={profile.manmade}>manmade.farhantaufiks.com</a>, for comparison.
      </p>
    </div>

    <h3 class="sub">The system I built around it</h3>
    <ul class="harness">
      {
        harness.map((h, i) => (
          <li>
            <span class="mono n">{String(i + 1).padStart(2, "0")}</span>
            <h4>{h.title}</h4>
            <p>{h.text}</p>
          </li>
        ))
      }
    </ul>

    <div class="split">
      <div class="verify">
        <h3 class="sub">How I check what comes back</h3>
        <ul class="check">
          {verify.map((v) => <li>{v}</li>)}
        </ul>
        <p class="aside">
          Knowing the drill is the job: which method, which check, which order. The typing is the
          cheap part now.
        </p>
      </div>

      <figure class="prompt">
        <figcaption class="mono">how this page was made · 2 prompts</figcaption>
        <div class="turn">
          <p class="mono who">v1 · me</p>
          <blockquote>
            "Create a website to introduce me, as Earth Science and Comp Science. I won't give
            specific instructions. Base it on what I do, how I talk to you in other sessions, my
            background, LinkedIn and CV."
          </blockquote>
          <p class="mono res">→ Claude: concept, stack (Astro), copy, repo split, nginx, TLS, deploy</p>
        </div>
        <div class="turn">
          <p class="mono who">v2 · me, after review</p>
          <blockquote>
            "This only covers my CV, not what I actually do. You know my work from other sessions.
            And I still verify the work. Don't undersell it."
          </blockquote>
          <p class="mono res">→ Claude: re-read 100+ project memories, rewrote the eDOT story and this section, with nothing under NDA</p>
        </div>
        <p class="moral">The first draft was fine. Fine wasn't the bar, so it went back.</p>
      </figure>
    </div>

    <div class="session">
      <h3 class="sub">Same session, before this page</h3>
      <ol class="log mono">
        {sameSession.map((s) => <li>{s}</li>)}
      </ol>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

<style>
  .claude {
    background: var(--bg-2);
    border-block: 1px solid var(--rule);
  }
  .sub {
    font-size: 1.4rem;
    margin-bottom: 16px;
  }
  .harness {
    list-style: none;
    margin: 0 0 48px;
    padding: 0;
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: repeat(4, minmax(0, 1fr));
    gap: 14px;
  }
  .harness li {
    background: var(--surface);
    border: 1px solid var(--rule);
    border-top: 3px solid var(--ochre);
    border-radius: 10px;
    padding: 18px;
    display: grid;
    align-content: start;
    gap: 8px;
  }
  .harness .n {
    color: var(--ink-3);
  }
  h4 {
    margin: 0;
    font-family: var(--serif);
    font-weight: 500;
    font-size: 1.2rem;
    line-height: 1.15;
  }
  .harness p {
    color: var(--ink-2);
    font-size: 0.93rem;
  }
  .split {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: 1fr 1fr;
    gap: 28px;
    align-items: start;
  }
  .check {
    list-style: none;
    margin: 0;
    padding: 0;
    display: grid;
    gap: 10px;
    color: var(--ink-2);
  }
  .check li {
    padding-left: 26px;
    position: relative;
  }
  .check li::before {
    content: "✓";
    position: absolute;
    left: 2px;
    color: var(--moss);
    font-weight: 700;
  }
  .aside {
    margin-top: 24px;
    font-family: var(--serif);
    font-size: 1.2rem;
    font-style: italic;
  }
  .prompt {
    margin: 0;
    border-radius: 14px;
    overflow: hidden;
    border: 1px solid var(--rule);
    background: var(--surface);
  }
  figcaption {
    padding: 10px 18px;
    border-bottom: 1px solid var(--rule);
    color: var(--ink-3);
    display: flex;
    align-items: center;
    gap: 8px;
  }
  figcaption::before {
    content: "";
    width: 8px;
    height: 8px;
    border-radius: 50%;
    background: var(--moss);
  }
  .turn {
    padding: 18px 20px;
    border-bottom: 1px dashed var(--rule);
    display: grid;
    gap: 8px;
  }
  .who {
    color: var(--ochre);
  }
  blockquote {
    margin: 0;
    font-family: var(--serif);
    font-size: 1.1rem;
    line-height: 1.45;
    font-style: italic;
  }
  .res {
    color: var(--moss);
    font-size: 0.74rem;
  }
  .moral {
    padding: 16px 20px 20px;
    font-weight: 500;
  }
  .session {
    margin-top: 48px;
  }
  .log {
    margin: 0;
    padding: 18px 20px 18px 44px;
    background: var(--bg);
    border: 1px solid var(--rule);
    border-radius: 10px;
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: 1fr 1fr;
    gap: 10px 32px;
    color: var(--ink-2);
    font-size: 0.8rem;
    line-height: 1.5;
  }
  .log li::marker {
    color: var(--moss);
  }
  @media (max-width: 960px) {
    .harness {
      grid-template-columns: repeat(2, minmax(0, 1fr));
    }
  }
  @media (max-width: 860px) {
    .split,
    .log {
      grid-template-columns: 1fr;
    }
  }
  @media (max-width: 560px) {
    .harness {
      grid-template-columns: 1fr;
    }
  }
</style>
